---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Heading } from '../components/ui/Heading';
import { Container } from '../components/ui/Container';
import { Stack } from '../components/ui/Stack';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Chidi Onyema" description="Principal Backend Engineer. 10+ years building distributed systems. London-based, remote-friendly.">
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <Container size="prose">
      <Stack gap={12}>
        <div>
          <Heading variant="hero" level={1}>About me</Heading>
          <p class="text-xl text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-6">
            I'm Chidi — a backend engineer in London who builds the systems
            behind payments, orders, and financial platforms. The kind of
            systems where a bug means someone loses money.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-primary max-w-none">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Why I built this</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            Early in my career I watched a payment system silently drop transactions
            during a deploy. No errors, no alerts — customers were charged but orders
            never created. It took three days to find the root cause: a message broker
            restart wiped unconfirmed messages, and there was no outbox to recover them.
          </p>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            That experience shaped everything I've done since. I don't trust happy-path
            demos or architecture diagrams. I want to see the failure, trigger it myself,
            and verify the system recovers. That's why this portfolio is a live cluster
            you can actually break.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">What I focus on</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            The problems I care about are the ones that wake people up at 3am:
          </p>
          <ul class="text-secondary space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Transactions that span multiple services</strong> — making sure an order either completes fully or rolls back cleanly, with no orphaned charges or phantom inventory.</li>
            <li><strong>Failure recovery</strong> — when a service goes down mid-operation, the system compensates automatically. No manual database fixes.</li>
            <li><strong>Financial correctness</strong> — every payment, refund, and payout is accounted for with double-entry bookkeeping. The books balance or the build breaks.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated enforcement</strong> — 159 architecture rules and 50 custom analyzers run on every build. The patterns are not documented guidelines; they are compiler errors.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">This portfolio</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            The platform running this site is 8 .NET 9 microservices deployed on
            Fly.io, with PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, and Redis. Every demo you try
            sends real HTTP requests through the full stack. The
            <a href="https://github.com/chidionyema/haworks-platform" target="_blank" class="text-accent hover:underline">source code</a> is
            public — including the saga state machines, the outbox configuration,
            the architecture guards, and the CI pipeline.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Education</h2>
          <ul class="text-secondary space-y-2">
            <li><strong>AI and Machine Learning</strong> — Professional Certificate, Imperial College Business School (2024)</li>
            <li><strong>Computer Science BSc (Hons)</strong> — Queen Mary University of London</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Stack</h2>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 not-prose">
            {['C# / .NET 9', 'MassTransit', 'EF Core', 'PostgreSQL', 'RabbitMQ', 'Redis', 'Polly', 'HashiCorp Vault', 'Docker', 'Fly.io', 'OpenTelemetry', 'xUnit', 'Pact', 'Aspire'].map(tech => (
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface-warm border border-border rounded text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider font-mono text-muted">{tech}</span>
            ))}
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mt-8">Availability</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary">
            Available for contract engagements. London-based, comfortable fully
            remote. Happy to discuss day rate and scope.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold bg-primary text-base-inverse hover:bg-secondary transition-all">
              Get in touch
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </Stack>
    </Container>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
